<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A suite whose time is concentrated in one class, which is the case the timing fields exist
  for. Two classes: CameraTests is 4 tests at 20s each, GridTests is 4 at 2.5s. Summed test
  time is 90s inside 30s of wall clock, because xUnit runs collections in parallel and
  defaults to one collection per class. The two numbers are deliberately different here, and
  a fixture that made them agree would prove nothing.

  CameraTests carries a theory whose name includes its arguments, so aggregating by class
  cannot be done by trimming the test name: the class is joined from TestDefinitions on
  testId.
-->
